# Admin Help knowledge coverage

Admin Help answers only from the knowledge pack: curated chunks plus a page guide for every admin page group. It does not read live pages, and it does not call `adwiise-agent-service`.

## Page guides (one per admin page group)

- When the user asks from a page, the whole guide for that page is sent to the model as `currentPageGuide`; other pages' guide sections are retrievable chunks.
- Hand-reviewed guides: `MANUAL_PAGE_GUIDES` in [pageGuides.ts](mdc:src/lib/adminHelp/knowledge/pageGuides.ts) (Tenant Settings). A manual guide wins over a generated one.
- Generated guides: [pageGuides.generated.json](mdc:src/lib/adminHelp/knowledge/generated/pageGuides.generated.json), written by `npm run help:guides` from the page code (UI text, labels, limits, actions) with Bedrock. Never edit it by hand; review its diff in the PR.
- After changing any admin page UI, run `npm run help:guides` (regenerates only stale guides), then `npm run test:admin-help` (smoke checks, the 40-question eval in `scripts/admin-help-eval.json`, and the staleness check).
- Add an eval case to `scripts/admin-help-eval.json` when a real question gets a wrong answer.

## Call path

```
Admin Help chat
  → POST /api/admin/help-chat
  → retrieveAdminHelpKnowledge (keyword match on stamped chunks)
  → Bedrock InvokeModel (us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5, us-east-1)
```

- Knowledge files: [hubGuides.ts](mdc:src/lib/adminHelp/knowledge/hubGuides.ts), [routeMap.ts](mdc:src/lib/adminHelp/knowledge/routeMap.ts), [howTos.ts](mdc:src/lib/adminHelp/knowledge/howTos.ts), [operatorGuides.ts](mdc:src/lib/adminHelp/knowledge/operatorGuides.ts).
- `adwiise-agent-service` Bedrock config is image-text only (`BedrockImageTextService`).
- Retail Ask uses Spring → AI engine `POST /v1/chat` → the same model family, with a different prompt. Do not send Admin Help there.

## When a tile or module is added

1. Add the tile on [src/app/admin/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/admin/page.tsx) with `key`, `href`, `label`, and `summary`.
2. Add a hub guide row with the same `key`, a one-sentence summary of what the screen does, keywords a person would type, and `pathPrefixes`.
3. Add a route-map entry for that path. Put a longer path before a shorter parent so the longest prefix wins.
4. If the screen has steps or contact fields (email, phone, payer), add a how-to that names those fields. School staff email and phone stay on `/admin/school`, not Executive Committee.
5. Run the coverage check and read the printed summary. Do not ship a tile that prints `MISSING`.

```
node scripts/check-admin-help-coverage.mjs
```

The script prints every Admin Home tile, its path, and its summary, then says whether the hub guide and route map include it.

## School

`/admin/school` (`school-site`) covers Staff, Departments, Facilities, Activities, Pages, Highlights, and Fee invoices. Staff holds teacher email and phone. Fee invoices hold payer name, email, and phone.

Full guide: [AWS_Bedrock_AI_LLM_Admin_help_help_chat_knowledge_coverage.html](mdc:documentation/admin_help_chat/AWS_Bedrock_AI_LLM_Admin_help_help_chat_knowledge_coverage.html).

Vector database and RAG stay out of this design. Analysis: [AWS_Bedrock_AI_LLM_vector_database_RAG_analysis.html](mdc:documentation/admin_help_chat/AWS_Bedrock_AI_LLM_vector_database_RAG_analysis.html).
